@startuml
!theme plain
title Turnstone — Watch Tool Architecture

skinparam participant {
    BackgroundColor<<server>> #FFE0B2
    BackgroundColor<<storage>> #B3E5FC
    BackgroundColor<<session>> #C8E6C9
    BackgroundColor<<ui>> #E8EAF6
}

participant "ChatSession\n(session.py)" as Session <<session>>
participant "WatchRunner\n(watch.py)" as Runner <<server>>
participant "StorageBackend\n(SQLite / PostgreSQL)" as Storage <<storage>>
participant "WebUI / SSE\n(server.py)" as UI <<ui>>
participant "Model" as Model

== Create Phase ==

Session -> Session : _prepare_watch(action="create")
note right
  Validates:
  - command via is_command_blocked()
  - poll_every → parse_duration()
  - stop_on → validate_condition()
  - max watches limit (5)
  - duplicate name check
  needs_approval = True
end note

Session -> Storage : create_watch(watch_id, ws_id,\nnode_id, command, interval,\nstop_on, max_polls, next_poll)

Session --> UI : tool_result:\n"Watch 'pr-review' created"

== Poll Phase (WatchRunner daemon, every 15s) ==

Runner -> Storage : list_due_watches(now)
Storage --> Runner : due_watches[]
note right
  Filters:
  active=1 AND
  next_poll <= now AND
  node_id matches
end note

loop for each due watch

    Runner -> Runner : is_command_blocked()?
    alt blocked
        Runner -> Storage : update_watch(active=False)
    else safe

        Runner -> Runner : subprocess.run(command)
        note right
          timeout = tool_timeout
          start_new_session = True
          output truncated at 64KB
        end note

        Runner -> Runner : evaluate_condition(\nstop_on, output,\nexit_code, prev_output)
        note right
          **Variables:**
          output, data, exit_code,
          prev_output, changed

          **Safe builtins only:**
          len, str, int, sorted, ...
          No import/open/exec/eval

          **stop_on=None:**
          fires on change (skip 1st poll)
        end note

        alt condition fired OR max_polls reached
            Runner -> Runner : build_watch_reminder()
            Runner -> Runner : _dispatch_result(ws_id, reminder)
            Runner -> Storage : update_watch(\npoll_count++,\nlast_output, active=False)
        else not fired
            Runner -> Storage : update_watch(\npoll_count++,\nlast_output, next_poll)
        end

    end
end

== Dispatch Phase ==

note over Runner, Session
  **Three dispatch paths:**
end note

alt Path A: workstream active + idle
    Runner -> Session : dispatch_fn(reminder)\n→ NudgeQueue.enqueue(channel="any")
    Session -> Session : wake workstream\n→ send("")

else Path B: workstream active + busy
    Runner -> Session : dispatch_fn(reminder)\n→ NudgeQueue.enqueue(channel="any")
    note right
      In-flight worker drains the notice
      at its next user or tool seam.
    end note

else Path C: workstream not loaded
    Runner -> Runner : restore_fn(ws_id)
    note right
      1. persona and owner checks
      2. mgr.open_with_outcome(ws_id) — may evict
         another idle workstream; open in another
         process → retry later; no turns → watch ends
      3. opened here: unattended approval until
         the first client, set_watch_runner()
      4. already loaded: register its dispatch_fn
    end note
    Runner -> Session : restored dispatch_fn(reminder)\n→ NudgeQueue.enqueue(channel="any")
end

Session -> Session : drain notice into watch_triggered system turn
Session -> UI : system_turn(content=notice, meta=output snapshot)
note over Session, UI
  The card renders output from structured metadata.
  Metadata is invisible to the model.
end note
Session -> Model : metadata-only operator notice + read hint
Model -> Session : watch(action="read", name="<full watch id>")
Session -> Session : find delivered snapshot in active transcript
alt no active snapshot
    Session -> Storage : get_watch_snapshot(current ws_id, full watch id)
    Storage --> Session : snapshot from this workstream's persisted history
end
alt no delivered snapshot
    Session -> Storage : resolve own watch; read stored last_output
    Storage --> Session : watch row (including completed watches)
end
note right
  The snapshot is available before
  the runner's final row commit.
  Forks keep inherited snapshots.
  Compacted-source forks copy retained
  snapshots before the child's checkpoint.
  Persisted snapshots survive compaction.
  Condition exception details also
  stay out of operator notice text.
end note
Session -> Session : output guard (when enabled)
Session -> Model : tool result with command output

== Cancel / List ==

Session -> Storage : list_watches_for_ws(ws_id)
note right : action="list" (auto-approve)

Session -> Storage : update_watch(active=False)
note right : action="cancel" (auto-approve)

== Server Lifecycle ==

note over Runner, Storage
  **Startup:**
  1. WatchRunner created in main() with storage + node_id
  2. restore_fn = make_watch_restore_fn(manager)
  3. Initial workstream: session.set_watch_runner(runner)
  4. _lifespan(): runner.start() — daemon thread begins

  **New workstream:**
  session.set_watch_runner(runner) in create_workstream()
  → registers dispatch_fn for ws_id

  **Eviction / close:**
  session.close() → runner.remove_dispatch_fn(ws_id)
  Watches remain active in DB — WatchRunner uses restore_fn

  **Restart recovery:**
  Overdue watches fire ONE immediate poll
  next_poll updated to now + interval
  Normal cadence resumes

  **Shutdown:**
  _lifespan(): runner.stop() — joins thread
end note

== REST API ==

note over UI, Storage
  **GET /v1/api/watches[?ws_id=X]**
  List active watches (for node or workstream)

  **POST /v1/api/watches/{watch_id}/cancel**
  Cancel a watch (sets active=False)

  Both require write scope
end note

@enduml
